+## ISSUE-010 — Annual P/E needs explicit timing and adjusted-price limits
+
+- **Date:** 2026-10-09
+- **Status:** Resolved
+- **Area:** Derived P/E history, chart labels, static tables and machine-readable copy.
+- **Symptoms:** Marketing generic P/E history from annual EPS and weekly adjusted prices could imply rolling TTM/forward ratios or information available to investors at each historical date.
+- **Cause:** The snapshot has annual facts, including later restatements, and the current US price export has no validated split-only closes. Filing and fiscal-end dates differ; adjusted closes can include dividend effects.
+- **Solution:** Match each annual EPS observation to an eligible close within 14 days on or before fiscal end, prefer split-only closes and label adjusted-close ratios approximate. Expose EPS basis, price date/type and filing dates; preserve gaps for non-positive EPS and missing prices. Explain retrospective timing, adjustment limitations, annual frequency and uncapped ratios in chart text, static summaries, guide and Markdown.
+- **Why this solution:** Reuses verified annual data and year-end price eligibility without inventing quarterly facts or consensus estimates. Keeps one existing page per stock plus one shared guide rather than duplicating financial-history pages.
+- **Verification:** Calculation tests cover basic/diluted differences, split-price precedence, adjusted fallback, 14-day boundary, stale/future prices, non-positive/missing EPS, uncapped ratios and filing dates. Generated HTML/Markdown/discovery tests pass and the raw company JSON is unchanged.
+- **Follow-up:** Obtain quarterly data or analyst estimates only if true TTM/forward P/E is requested. Validate price/EPS split alignment before making exact historical-ratio claims.
+- **References:** `web/calculations.js`, `web/pe.js`, `scripts/site.mjs`, `scripts/ai.mjs`, `tests/pe.test.js`, `tests/site.test.js`.
 
